  "title": "BEETL Competition 2021 Motor Imagery Dataset B — transfer learning benchmark",
  "description": "Beetl2021-B is a preprocessed 32-channel EEG dataset from the NeurIPS 2021 BEETL competition, built to benchmark transfer learning for motor imagery decoding. It contains recordings from 2 healthy subjects performing four-class motor imagery (left hand, right hand, feet, rest) at 200 Hz, totaling 1590 trials. The dataset supports evaluation of cross-subject and cross-dataset generalization and domain adaptation in brain-computer interfaces.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was acquired at 200 Hz from 32 channels placed around the motor cortex (standard 1005 montage) with online bandpass filtering (1-100 Hz). Data were bandpass filtered in the frequency domain (1-100 Hz) and segmented into 4-second trials. Visual cues indicated four motor imagery classes, and evaluation used block-wise 5-fold cross-validation with cross-subject and cross-dataset assessment.",
